In   -
Out  EasySocket
Type Module
Ver  1.16a
Max  16k

Define Workspace
 Name      socket
 Default   r11
  `next    !  the next socket in the chain
  `magic   !  a magical value
  `socket  !  the socket handle
  `addr    !  the address name
  `port    !  the port number
  `state   !  the state of the connection
  `buffer  !  buffer for incoming data
  `buflen  !  length of buffer
  `datalen !  length of data in buffer
  `domain  !  domainid marker

 Name      monitor
 Default   r10
  `mon_next   !  the next monitor block
  `mon_magic  !  another magical value
  `pollptr    !  pointer to the pollword
  `mon_domain !  domainid marker
  `mon_type   !  the monitor type
  `pollword   !  the pollword to modify when event
  (
  `mon_skt    !  the socket we're monitoring (type 0)
  )

 Name      module
 Default   r12
  `sockets  !  socket handles
  `monitors !  monitor blocks (OS_Upcall)
  `address  !4 address block
  `hostname !32 space for a hostname (128 chars ok ?)
End Workspace

Define Module
 Name      EasySocket
 Author    Justin Fletcher
 SWIs
  Prefix   ESocket
  Base     &51C00
   0       ConnectToHost     swi_connecttohost
   1       CheckState        swi_checkstate
   2       Forget            swi_forget
   3       SendLine          swi_sendline
   4       ReadLine          swi_readline
   5       SendData          swi_senddata
   6       ReadData          swi_readdata
   7       Closed            swi_closed
   8       Listen            swi_listen
   9       Accept            swi_accept
   10      ConnectionName    swi_connectionname
   11      Monitor           swi_monitor
   12      ResetMonitor      swi_resetmonitor
   13      OurAddress        swi_ouraddress
   14      DecodeState       swi_decodestate
   15      TaskAssociation   swi_association
   16      ConnectToAddr     swi_connecttoaddr
   17      TheirAddress      swi_theiraddress
 End SWIs
 Services
  WimpCloseDown        svc_wimpclosedown ; to trap closing tasks
 End Services
 Events
  Internet         event_inet
  Buffer_Entering  event_entering
 End Events
 Commands
  Name     ESockets
  Help     *ESockets will list the connections currently being used.
  Code     com_esockets

  Name     EMonitors
  Help     *EMonitors will list the monitors currently active.
  Code     com_emonitors
 End Commands
 PostFilter
  Name     ESockets TWInput
  Task     -
  Accept   UserMessage
  Accept   UserMessageRecorded
  Code     jfilter_twcheck
 End PostFilter
 Final     finalise
 Workspace *`len_module
End Module

Pre
 S_Lookup=1:REM We're looking the address up
 S_Connecting=2:REM We're trying to connect
 S_Listening=3:REM We're listening for a connection
 S_Connected=4:REM We're connected !
 S_NoSuchHost=-1
 S_ResolveFailure=-2
 S_ResolveError=-3
 S_NoSockets=-4
 S_Unreachable=-5
 S_NotListening=-6
 S_BindError=-7
 S_NooneThere=-8
 MagicVal=&feef1ef0:REM Fee Fie Fo...
 MagicVal_Monitor=&beeffeed:REM Ah, the reason for dying all the time
 InitialBuffer=256
 MaximumBuffer=1024*32
 LowLimit=&8000:REM Minimum that a descriptor block may be
End Pre

#Rem off
